.TH SMDIM 1
.SH NAME
smdim \- dimension a drawing view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smdim
[
.B \-s
.I scale
] [
.B \-u
.IR unit [, unit ]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Smdim
reads a view from
.IR smview (1)
on the standard input and writes it in inches on the paper at
.I scale
(default 1), with the datum (the lower left corner of the view) at the
origin, and with its dimensions and callouts, whose sizes are in the
units of
.B \-u
.RB ( in
or
.BR mm ,
.B in
by default), the second after each in brackets.
Fill, line, arc and poly records are kept, without their features; a
region
.B fill cut
I of a section, the faces of part I that the plane cuts, becomes
.BI "fill hatch" " angle gap" :
its section lines, thin, at the angle of the part, 45 degrees for part
0, 135 for part 1, then 30, 120, 60 and 150 and round again, and
.I gap
inches apart (.08 unless a record
.B hatching
says); the view record is given the scale; thick and radius records
are passed through in mm.
A record may have any number of fields.
The sides of each coat become lines of kind p (phantom), and a coat that
is a rectangle along the axes gets a hatch, unless a record
.B unhatched
names its material, but a coat of a face of a solid, whose sides are its edges, gets neither; a coat of a material of a
texture record gets its mark, a text in its middle, but the coats of
faces of one texture one mark in the view, at the free place nearest
the middle of the largest of them that has room, none if none has;
each texture record goes on, as
.BI texture " mark callout" ,
for the notes of
.IR smsheet (1).
These records are added:
.PP
.RS
.nf
line c v X0 Y0 X1 Y1     center mark
thin X0 Y0 X1 Y1
text X Y ANGLE ALIGN HEIGHT STRING...
arrow X Y DX DY
dot X Y
flag X Y N
hatch X0 Y0 X1 Y1
clear X0 Y0 X1 Y1        background of a text on a hatch
crowd D
far N
dim ord|hole|insert|radius|lin|pitch|bend ...
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I Align
is
.BR l ,
.B c
or
.B r
(the place of X Y in the text, at half its height).
In strings, %%c is the diameter sign, %%v the countersink sign,
%%d the degree sign, and %%p plus or minus.
.I Crowd
is the greatest distance of an ordinate text from its place;
.I far
is the number of long leaders.
Dim records repeat the text of each dimension, for tests.
.PP
Dimensions are ordinates from the datum, in inches to three decimals
without the leading zero or in mm to two: to the far end, to each hole,
to each edge of a cut-out, each side of a coat and each center line,
and to other edges not close to these; a poly record has none.
Equal holes share one callout with their count and pitch, and arcs of
one radius share one, but arcs that make a whole circle none.
A hole callout gives the diameter, as %%c.089, and the depth of a blind
hole, as X .230 DEEP, or THRU if it has a countersink; for a thread,
the designation and THRU or its depth, as
.BR "4-40 UNC-2B X .230 DEEP" ,
and not the drill; a countersink adds a line, as
.BR "%%v%%c.110 X 82%%d" ,
with FARSIDE if it is at the far side.
The count ends the last line, after a comma but on a plain hole.
The holes of inserts get no callout of their size: the inserts of one
type on one side share one, by the record
.BI inserts " format"
.RI ( draw (5)),
whose %n is the count, %t the type and %s the side, NEAR or FAR, in
capitals; with none, INSTALL %n %t, %s SIDE.
Bend lines of the flat view are marked UP or DOWN, with the angle.
No text overlaps another, and no leader crosses a text or a leader.
.PP
These records after the view change the result:
.PP
.RS
.nf
drop FEATURE [x|y|d|r]   omit the dimensions of a feature
lin x|y A B [PLUS MINUS] linear dimension, with tolerances
leader X Y STRING...     note with a dot at X Y, inches from the datum
flag X Y N [STRING...]   box of note N, with text after it
hatch X0 Y0 X1 Y1        hatching across the material there
inserts FORMAT           the callout of a group of inserts
hatching GAP             the gap between section lines, inches
unhatched MATERIAL...    the coats of these get no hatch
.fi
.RE
.PP
After a line
.BI #line " n name" ,
messages about the records that follow give line
.I n
of
.IR name .
.PP
The ends of a
.B lin
stand at an ordinate, or at any visible edge of the view square to its
axis, of the outline, a cut-out, a bend or a coat, or at a hole.
.PP
.B drop
leaves out all the dimensions of the feature of the part that the
view records name
.RI ( sm (5)),
or only its ordinates on one axis, its hole callouts or its radii.
The lengths of the records are in inches, as
.IR smsheet (1)
works them out from the drawing file.
.SH EXAMPLES
smview top part.st | smdim \-s .5 \-u mm,in >top.dim
.SH SEE ALSO
smview(1), smsheet(1), smdraw(1), draw(5)
